主要终点:
Functional status at 3 months after ischemic stroke

Functional status assessment at 3 months after ischemic stroke, using the modified Rankin Scale (mRS), analyzed on an ordinal scale (0-6), to measure the degree of dependence/functional impairment.

Score ranges:

0-no residual symptoms (better outcome);

1. no significant disability;
2. slight disability;
3. moderate disability;
4. moderately severe disability;
5. severe disability;
6. death (worse outcome).

